title: Ministry of Labour
card-image: img/cards/labor_affairs.svg?v=2
subtitle: Strike arbitration, the eight-hour day and the factory committees.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: coalition_affairs
view-if: labor_affairs_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; labor_affairs_timer = 3

[? if dix < 17 : The Ministry of Labour, in the Menshevik Skobelev's hands, handles the strikes that sweep every industrial city. ?][? if dix >= 17 and dix < 20 : The Ministry of Labour, now in the hands of the Menshevik Gvozdev, a metalworker who sat on the war industries committee, handles the strikes that sweep every industrial city. ?][? if dix >= 20 : The Ministry of Labour, in socialist hands since 1917, handles the lay-offs and the strikes of the Republic's industrial cities. ?][? if dix < 12 : The laundresses of Petrograd are out, and the Donbas mine owners are threatening a lockout. ?][? if dix >= 12 and dix < 20 : The autumn has brought the largest strikes of the year: the railwaymen, the Moscow leather workers, the textile mills of the Central Industrial Region. ?][? if dix >= 20 and dix < 48 : With the army being demobilised, the factories are cutting shifts and closing for want of fuel and orders. ?][? if dix >= 48 : Production is recovering slowly, and the workers want their share of the recovery before the employers have taken it. ?] Employers want order and the factory committees want control. The socialists are both the workers' parties and parties of government.

- @arbitrate: Arbitrate the strikes through conciliation boards.
- @committees: Legalise the factory committees and the eight-hour day.
- @circular: Forbid the factory committees to interfere with management (Skobelev's circular).
- @easy_discard

@arbitrate
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 1});
RO.add(Q, {ruble: 2, rel_kad: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -1);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 1);
!}

[? if dix < 12 : Conciliation boards settled the laundresses' strike in Petrograd and the worst of the disputes in the Donbas. ?][? if dix >= 12 and dix < 20 : Conciliation boards settled the railwaymen's dispute and, at last, the long strike of the Moscow leather workers. ?][? if dix >= 20 : Conciliation boards settled the worst disputes over the lay-offs in Petrograd and the Urals. ?] The employers are grateful. The factory committees are less so.

@committees

How should the party go about it? Cautiously, with compromises, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. In full, it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can carry it out and break its opponents.

- @committees_slow: Go about it cautiously, with compromises.
- @committees_decree: Carry it out in full.
- @committees_force: Carry it out in full, and break any opposition by force.

@committees_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 5, railway: 2});
RO.add(Q, {ruble: -3, rel_kad: -4, bolshevik: -1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 3);
}, "Legalise the factory committees and the eight-hour day");
!}

The committees are recognised in law and the eight-hour day is guaranteed. The factory owners say they will close the plants. A few have. (It was done cautiously, with compromises.)



@committees_decree
subtitle: All that it says. Its opponents will answer.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'decree', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 5, railway: 2});
RO.add(Q, {ruble: -3, rel_kad: -4, bolshevik: -1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 3);
}, "Legalise the factory committees and the eight-hour day");
!}

The committees are recognised in law and the eight-hour day is guaranteed. The factory owners say they will close the plants. A few have.



@committees_force
view-if: bol_regime = 0
choose-if: strength >= 18
subtitle: Your chance of breaking each camp it angers: Kadets [+ odds_kad +]%. Any camp under 45% is too strong for you, and is left alone.
unavailable-subtitle: We lack the force and the allies to break the opposition.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'force', () => {
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 5, railway: 2});
RO.add(Q, {ruble: -3, rel_kad: -4, bolshevik: -1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 3);
}, "Legalise the factory committees and the eight-hour day");
!}

The committees are recognised in law and the eight-hour day is guaranteed. The factory owners say they will close the plants. A few have. [+ law_text +]

@circular
on-arrival: {!
RO.boost(Q, {workers: -4});
RO.add(Q, {ruble: 2, bolshevik: 3, rel_kad: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 4);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, -1);
!}

[? if dix < 17 : Skobelev's circular forbade the committees from interfering with management. ?][? if dix >= 17 : Skobelev's old circular, reissued over his successor's signature, forbade the committees from interfering with management. ?] The Bolsheviks have printed it in full, with their own comments.
